# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in.  NEVER commit a filled-in copy.
#   cp .env.example .env.local
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Supabase: project settings --------------------------------------------
# Both of these are safe to expose to the browser (the anon key is protected
# by Row Level Security, NOT by being secret).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# --- Supabase: SERVER ONLY -------------------------------------------------
# This key BYPASSES Row Level Security. It must only ever be read inside
# Route Handlers / server code.
#
# Guard rails (enforced in code):
#   * `src/lib/supabase/server.ts` throws if this is imported into a client bundle
#   * `src/lib/env.ts` validates it is set only when `serverEnv` is accessed
#   * nothing under `NEXT_PUBLIC_` may reference it
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key

# --- Internal scheduler ----------------------------------------------------
# Required at RUNTIME, not at build time: `serverEnv()` (src/lib/env.ts) demands
# at least 32 characters, and it is invoked by `createAdminClient()` on every
# API route, so leaving it unset or too short 500s the whole app.
# Generate with:  openssl rand -hex 32
#
# Phase advancement is lazy and also runs on room requests. Production should
# additionally invoke these authenticated endpoints once per minute so rooms
# with no traffic still recover expired work and finish pending actions:
#   POST /api/internal/pending-actions/recover
#   POST /api/internal/hunter-shots/recover
# Authorization: Bearer <SCHEDULER_SECRET>
SCHEDULER_SECRET=replace-with-32-byte-random-hex

# --- Optional: direct Postgres, used by integration/RLS tests only ---------
# Optional in the schema; the application never reads it. Tests gate on it and
# skip rather than pass vacuously when it is absent.
# Needs the direct connection string (port 5432), NOT the pooler (6543).
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/postgres

# --- Optional: local stack script ONLY (scripts/supastack-local.sh) --------
# NOT read by the Next.js app — nothing under src/ references SUPASTACK_*.
# PostgREST's login role. The `authenticator` role is not created anywhere in
# this repo yet (see docs/LOCAL-STACK.md), so point this at a role that exists.
# SUPASTACK_PGRST_DB_USER=authenticator
# SUPASTACK_PGRST_DB_PASSWORD=
# SUPASTACK_DB=werewolf_e2e
#
# Prefer putting these in a git-ignored `.supastack.env` instead: the script
# sources that file before falling back to the defaults above.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tunables are NOT env vars for the MVP. They live in src/lib/game/settings.ts
# so they are versioned and unit-tested. Only deployment secrets belong here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
